th it can't help  but win me over in the end and he really  is such an essential aspect to the  series he and Hinata are more like her  protagonists and I can't wait to see  where their partnership takes them in  future seasons but I actually don't  think there's a single character on the  karasuno team that I dislike probably  the person I feel most neutral about  Asuka Shima but that's very much because  that's how his character has been  betrayed up until this point you know  the kind of neutral apathetic being who  after his initial role in the first few  episodes has spent the rest of the  series just kind of being there he does  have his moments and I'm sure that he'll  probably have his own story thread going  on at some stage in the future but for  now he's the one who I generally care  about the least which is actually very  complementary to the rest of the cast  many of whom I love to death already  another favorite of mine is nishinoya  because it's always nice to see an  energetic powerhouse and someone who is  short in a sport that is primarily  dominated by Giants he also has a really  nice pin on him which is his focus on  being a liberal but I have to say that  some of the most charming characters in  the series are the ones who see very  little action on the court at all and  the first person who comes to my tía is  suka wada  i spent a lot of season one feeling  terribly sorry for him because being a  setter was his thing he's clearly  passionate about volleyball but when you  have a genius like cocky ama coming  along it's hard to deny that he is the  one who should be playing the set a role  but thanks to the sheer brilliance of IQ  characters like this do kit that you  recognition and sugawara x' moment where  he is brought onto the court to replace  cocky ama is one of my fondest memories  in the series thus far showing that hard  work does pay off in fur  while he completely dominated the game  as a result plus he also works as a  brilliant contrast to carry Amma  really showing us the versatility of a  setter and how different mindsets can  put unique spins on the position which  to be fair the setters of every other  team in the series also do this quite  effectively but it was much nicer to see  it coming from sugawara because of how  he dealt with the exact same team that  Kageyama had to work with and i could  probably go on and on and over every  member of the team like this but I'd be  here all day however the one final  character I do want to give some focus  to is Yamaguchi so if Hinata and  Kageyama are the driving force behind  the series and Yamaguchi certainly  represents its heart and soul  he is average in almost every way  imaginable he almost never gets on the  court and the one time I remember he did  he failed immediately and was taken off  fail being subjective of course because  I guess he didn't serve his purpose but  at the same time he just keeps going  regardless which in some ways is so much  more admirable than Hinata or Kageyama  because his struggle seems infinitely  greater than theirs he does have the  same desire that everyone else on the  team has and he works hard to achieve it  he just doesn't have the ridiculous  talent or physicality that everyone else  sports which is why I'm Iguchi is so so  important because he is the eyes of the  average viewer and I hope more than  anything that at some stage he does get  a real moment to shine because I have no  doubt that he will be working hard  enough to deserve it what I will also  say about haikyuu is that it is  incredibly addictive due to its format  especially when it really gets going in  the second half of the first series like  as soon as the tournament began it was  almost impossible to stop watching  episodes I felt like I needed to know  the outcome of every game and even after  a game was finished I found myself far  too eager to devour the next one and two  just keep pursuing things to their  natural conclusion I think that is part  of the general appeal of tournament sir  and why they tend to pop up and shown in  series even when they're not sport  related but one potential negative I  will say though is that the locations in  high Q can become just a little bit  stagnant which is something that I guess  can't really be helped because due to  the nature of the story the characters  will either be training which will take  place in the gym or they'll be playing a  match which will take place in another  gym elsewhere and while the gyms do have  subtle differences it can end up feeling  more or less the same and that would be  an incredibly detracting factor if the  characters weren't strong enough to take  command of the series without that  visual backing however they are good  enough to stand alone so there's that  personally I do wish that the aesthetics  of the series did have a bit more flow  I would love it if every gym or  tournament arena and a radically  different appearance but at the same  time that wouldn't really fit the style  that the series is presenting which is  undoubtedly realism I mean yes there are  moments in play where Hinata and the  other characters will pull off some  absurd moves that look completely  impossible to achieve in reality but  other than that thank you is very  grounded in the real world and with that  in mind I guess it does make sense to  have these realistic locations but do  more or less look the same like standard  gymnasiums would but I can't help but  wonder what would have happened if  haikyuu took more of a food war style  focus though where it took this  realistic activity and pushed it to its  stylistic limits whilst being able to  maintain a solid character focus it may  have helped it probably would have  hindered and I guess in the end it  doesn't really matter because this  series as is managed to hook me  regardless it doesn't stop haikyuu from  taking you to deep emotional places all  over the spectrum in fact quite possibly  the most impactful moment to season one  for me is after car sooner loses the  inter-high tournament and the whole team  were at a restaurant in complete silence  with tears streaming down their eyes and  just being told to eat and rebuild their  muscles it was such a bittersweet moment  I mean mostly bitter I guess but it was  coated in hope because the general idea  is that from this moment they will only  get stronger this defeat was a necessary  step in the continued growth of the team  and that next time they would go further  and further and I love that and oddly  enough all of this really struck me  because one of the things that I think  made me so hesitant about sports anime  is the concept that winning is  everything  and even then I guess I do have to admit  that most characters in haiku are  heavily focused on victory but honestly  that is one of the things that made me  fall out of love with soccer and  basketball that overwhelming drive to  win was imposed on us by the courage and  other teammates and I was always more  interested in having fun with what I was  doing rather than looking only towards  victory so I was a bit surprised how  easily I got on board with something  that I'd very much been fighting against  my entire sporting life but I suppose  that is the greatness of IQ really I get  to live vicariously through these driven  fictional characters and in the meantime  I can use my life to live it exactly how  I see fit but I still get the experience  of the profound highs and lows that  victory and defeat deliver through this  brilliant series so I am a bit sad that  I've put it off for this long but at the  same time I'm incredibly excited to  watch more high Q and possibly even  explore other great sports  which you know if you have any more  recommendations do feel free to drop  them in the comments below but for now  to conclude I have to say that I am very  impressed with what Hank you has to  offer thus far it's done a wonderful job  of crafting characters who are easy to  empathize with and be able to truly feel  their experiences as a result it's a  fantastic ensemble piece and I can't  even begin to imagine the growth that  everyone is going to undertake over what  is a two more full series in two films  ah I've got to go so we're going to  leave this here so that I can go and  delve into more haikyuu and that pretty  much does it for my initial thoughts and  thank you if you enjoyed this video and  the content this channel produced in  general then please do consider donating  to the new world review patreon because  the support of all of your amazing  people is what continues to make this  channel possible and if patreon isn't  quite your style then please do leave  this video a like share or subscribe  because it also helps support this  channel an incredible amount and if  you'd like to join the fun at any time  then please do head over to my discord  server where a wide array of shonali and  rey takes place on a daily basis and  finally please do comment with your  thoughts on haikyuu  this has been the new world review and  I'll see you next time

